cartridge "STARLIGHT/CLAUDE FOR AMY STUDIO/2026"

' STARLIGHT
' An original puzzle game for the ColecoVision, written in Amy by Claude (an
' AI made by Anthropic) for Amy Studio, 2026.
'
' Dusk. Twenty-five stars sleep in the sky. Wake one and it wakes its four
' neighbours too - or puts the awake ones back to sleep. Wake every star
' and the sky draws a picture. Ten nights, each a little harder.
'
' Controls (either joystick): the stick moves between the stars; the left
' button wakes the star you point at (and its neighbours); the right button
' starts the night again. Keypad not used.
'
' Liberties and sources: the puzzle is the classic "lights out" kind (made
' famous by Tiger Electronics' Lights Out, 1995); the stars, the nights,
' the pictures in the sky, the music and the intro picture are new. Each
' night is made by pressing a few stars of a fully awake sky, so every
' night can be solved, and the fewest moves are known.
' The intro is a 120-colour picture (kit/c120, `120 colors on`).
'
' House rules kept: columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the frame
' loop is protected from the NMI (Frame1); the tune plays once (TzLeft).

' Amy workaround: with `120 colors on`, small programs have their first
' user bytes on the joypad buffers (reported, bugs/120c-ram-overlap). This
' game's layout is larger and not hit; the four bytes stay as a guard.
u8 JoyGap[4]

